+\ Copy u bytes starting at c-addr1 to c-addr2, a byte at a time in
+\ ascending order - an overlap moving up repeats bytes, as it always has.
+\ The two addresses are one double, moved on together by 1 1 D+ (it cannot
+\ carry: that needs an address at the top of memory); the copy stops at
+\ the source's end, kept on the return stack - 11 operations a byte, not
+\ 19 (the audit, Iteration 156).
