+\ -(1,1) as a double, so -1 -2 D+ takes 1 from each - the low cell would
+\ borrow only from address 0. The copy stops below the source's first
+\ byte, kept on the return stack - 11 operations a byte, not 19 (the audit,
+\ Iteration 156); HEADER8 moves every new name up with it.
+   DUP IF
+    >R OVER -1 + R> SWAP >R
+    -1 + DUP D+
+    BEGIN OVER C@ OVER C! -1 -2 D+ OVER R@ = UNTIL
+    R>
    THEN
-   2DROP DROP
+   DROP 2DROP
